erratum the row this lap booked was renumbered when it landed on 20260908.191521 -- it was booked from a local read while this log sat parked in a round-open stash, and by the time it landed the anointed spine had spent that number on another stamp. The stamp above is the key and has not moved; the shelf paths in the file fields below are the renamed ones.
scope one keystone -- the parked rish_report_bound guard family recovered, re-proven and landed, its row renumbered and folded; two reds closed on the way
status GREEN -- rish_report_bound witness GREEN and control pass=15 fail=0 on metal, index_row_bound verdict=ok after repair, reds_spine_derive verdict=ok rebindings=0, the REDS pin back under bound; the cold open incomplete by my own mid-run checkout and named rather than quoted, with the hot pass standing as this lap's reading
recommend keep-going -- recover stash@{3} next, the release-walk row and its fold shelf: it is the last of my parked laps, and its shelf claims rows-594 which the spine has long since bound elsewhere, so it wants a fresh number read before anything is written.
